o do by Sugrīva, Hanumān has destroyed Räkşasas and burnt Lankā; and this he did of himself like a good servant.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-1-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6001006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3574e04b47b04848fd0b00090f9d3d9575d198c3bc9c2a4c4672dd8833f87a56","compact":"3469df91ef6dcc3ead23490c553bcb0cb6d605e8a0e9026aa7e54ca879a74821","nasal":"3469df91ef6dcc3ead23490c553bcb0cb6d605e8a0e9026aa7e54ca879a74821"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-1-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":1,"verse":7,"english":"That servant who, being entrusted with a hard task, after having accomplished it, do another work in pursuance of (the prescribed business), is the best of men.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-1-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6001007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"478fc8f7eec38ba7d28c9997919daee6ea401a74edf7bbe5da87ece835a5d489","compact":"d7036b05ddaa56639285d77e3b06f5ff74a14026068367d856cab9e61decff88","nasal":"d7036b05ddaa56639285d77e3b06f5ff74a14026068367d856cab9e61decff88"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-1-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":1,"verse":8,"english":"That servant is middling, who, deputed to any task,* do not albeit capable, perform any other work which may be dear to the king. *i.e. performing the entrusted work. That servant who, entrusted with any work of the king do not, although competent, heedfully accomplish the same, has been called the worst.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-1-8","DUTT-6-1-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6001008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d954a70a